2026-10-21 22:43:52 GMT Daylight Time | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow: {"type": "AI", "text": "I'd be happy to recommend a fantasy book! To provide a more tailored suggestion, could you please tell me:\n\n1. What sub-genre of fantasy you prefer (e.g., high fantasy, urban fantasy, dark fantasy, epic fantasy, etc.)?\n2. Any specific themes or elements you enjoy (e.g., magic systems, political intrigue, coming-of-age stories, dragons, etc.)?\n3. Any books or authors you've enjoyed in the past?\n\nIf you're not sure, here's a general recommendation to start with:\n\n**\"The Name of the Wind\" by Patrick Rothfuss** – This is a beautifully written coming-of-age story set in a richly detailed world. It follows the life of Kvothe, a magically gifted young man, as he recounts his transformation from a traveling trouper to a notorious magician. The prose is lyrical, the magic system is intricate, and the story is deeply engaging. It's the first book in the *Kingkiller Chronicle* series.\n\nIf you're looking for something else, let me know your preferences!"}
